{
  "company_name": "ChemFlow Industries",
  "industry": "Chemicals & Materials",
  "use_case": "Chemical product demand forecasting and inventory optimization",
  "space_title": "ChemFlow Industries - Demand Forecasting & Inventory Optimization 📈",
  "space_description": "**Scenario:** You own the supply chain at ChemFlow Industries, balancing 20 chemical SKUs across six plants while feedstock prices swing 20-40% year over year. Sales is screaming about backorders, the CFO is screaming about working capital tied up in safety stock, and your demand model keeps missing on the high-velocity solvents and polymers. Where is your forecast drifting badly enough to be both starving customers and bloating inventory at the same time?\n\n**Questions:**\n\n1. Showcase the different visualization options with interesting aspects of the dataset (agent)\n2. What is my current order book composition by product category, customer segment, and fulfillment status? (agent)\n3. Which products have both the worst forecast accuracy (actual vs forecasted kg) and a Critical or Low reorder status right now? (agent)",
  "schema_basename": "chem_demand_forecast",
