  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports demand forecasting and inventory optimization for a multi-plant specialty and basic chemicals producer (solvents, polymers, specialty chemicals, coatings, adhesives). Stakeholders include the Supply Chain VP (fill rate, OTIF, days inventory), the CFO (working capital tied up in inventory, forecast bias impact on revenue), and Plant Managers (safety-stock policy, reorder timing). Chemical demand is materially exposed to feedstock price volatility, downstream automotive / construction / pharma cycles, and seasonal solvent / coating demand patterns.\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Forecast accuracy = total_actual_qty_kg / NULLIF(total_forecasted_qty_kg, 0); MAPE benchmark ~25-30% at SKU-plant-month grain for specialty chemicals\n- Fill rate = fulfilled_order_count / total_order_count; target ≥ 98% for industrial customers\n- Backorder rate = backorder_count / total_order_count; >2% is a churn warning sign\n- Days of supply = days_of_supply on inventory_positions; healthy band 30-60 days for finished chemicals, 15-30 for high-velocity SKUs\n- Safety stock coverage = on_hand_qty_kg / NULLIF(safety_stock_kg, 0); below 1.0 = below safety stock\n- Total order value = SUM(order_value_usd); avg unit price = AVG(unit_price_usd) per kg\n- Critical / Low reorder counts indicate stockout risk requiring expediting\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - chemical_orders_metrics (source: chemical_orders) — dims: order_date, product_category, customer_segment, plant_id, fulfillment_status; measures: total_order_value_usd, total_order_quantity_kg, fulfilled_order_count, total_order_count, backorder_count, avg_unit_price_usd, unique_product_count, max_order_quantity_kg.\n  - demand_forecasts_metrics (source: demand_forecasts) — dims: forecast_month, product_category, plant_id, model_version; measures: total_forecasted_qty_kg, total_actual_qty_kg, total_forecasted_revenue, total_actual_revenue, forecast_record_count, unique_product_count, max_forecasted_quantity_kg.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. product_id, product_name, on_hand_qty_kg, safety_stock_kg, days_of_supply, reorder_status).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
